# ===== Supabase Postgres =====
# The Next.js app is READ-ONLY over the DB (Drizzle + postgres-js). n8n owns all writes,
# using its OWN Supabase service-role key configured inside n8n -- NOT here. So the app needs
# only the two connection strings below; no anon / service-role / NEXT_PUBLIC keys required.
#
# Where to get them: Supabase Dashboard -> [Connect] (top bar) -> connection string.
# Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your DB password (Project Settings -> Database -> reset if needed).
# Copy them verbatim from the dialog -- host/region/username differ per project; don't hand-build.

# App runtime -> TRANSACTION pooler, port 6543. (postgres-js runs prepare:false + max:1; see src/db/index.ts)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"

# drizzle-kit only (pull / generate / migrate) -> SESSION pooler, port 5432.
# NOT the "Direct connection" (db.<ref>.supabase.co) -- that's IPv6-only and fails on Vercel/CI.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
